---
args: { dossier: ChangeOrderDossier }
returns: ChangeOrderImpactPacket
---
1. Bind authority = reconcileInstructionAuthority(dossier.instruction, dossier.writtenConfirmations, dossier.fieldReports, dossier.evidence). Preserve a disputed verbal instruction and contemporaneous event separately; work performed before commercial approval is an event record, not retroactive authorization.
2. Bind scope = isolateChangedDrawingAreas(dossier.drawingRevisions, dossier.evidence). A drawing revision limited to one area cannot flow into unchanged areas unless an explicit dependency supports it.
3. Bind dependencyTrace = traceChangeDependencies(scope, dossier.dependencies, dossier.evidence). Bind dependencies = dependencyTrace.reachablePackageIds. Use traversedEdges and unresolvedEdges to expose exactly which package paths are evidence-backed and which require review.
4. Bind schedule = testAvailableFloat(dossier.schedule, dependencies). Compare the changed critical path with the supplied activity durations and float; state assumptions and missing predecessor data. Do not assert delay where available float absorbs the change.
5. Bind costs = removeDuplicateChangeAttribution(dossier.costItems, dossier.fieldReports). Attribute each supported work item once across overlapping changes; preserve actual cost evidence even if approval is disputed.
6. Bind packet = { caseId: dossier.caseId, authority, affectedAreas: scope.affectedAreas, unaffectedAreas: scope.unaffectedAreas, scopeBlockers: scope.unresolvedAreas, dependencies, dependencyBlockers: dependencyTrace.unresolvedEdges.map(edge => edge.blocker), floatAnalysis: schedule.findings, nonDuplicatedCostItems: costs.acceptedIds, excludedDuplicateCostIds: costs.duplicateIds, costBlockers: costs.unresolvedIds, proposalStatus: authority.confirmed && scope.unresolvedAreas.length == 0 && dependencyTrace.unresolvedEdges.length == 0 && schedule.blockers.length == 0 && costs.unresolvedIds.length == 0 ? "review-required" : "needs-review", commitAllowed: false }.
7. Bind sourceKey from every value that can change a judgment: instruction ID/version, issuer, issue time, requestedChange and authorityScope; each confirmation's instructionRef, signer, receivedAt, scope, authorityRef and disputed status; each field event's eventId, package, time, description, actualCost and evidenceRef; each drawing's ID, revision, changed and unchanged areas, referenceOnly flag and evidenceRef; every schedule activity's IDs, predecessors, planned dates, remaining duration, available float and affected status; every cost item's ID, work package, change, quantity, rate, evidenceRef and overlapGroup; every dependency's source, target, relation and evidenceRef; and evidence IDs, versions, status, supports and contradictions. This source key identifies the exact source edition and must change when any authority, scope, field event, schedule or cost basis changes.
8. Restore state = dossier.state or { revision: 0, currentSourceKey: null, editions: [], attributedCostIds: [], unresolvedCostIds: [] }. If an edition with the exact sourceKey exists, reuse its version and preserve state unchanged. Otherwise append an immutable ChangeOrderEdition containing sourceKey, version state.revision + 1, the exact source records, packet.authority, affectedAreas, unaffectedAreas, scopeBlockers, dependencies, dependencyBlockers, dependencyTrace.unresolvedEdges, floatAnalysis, nonDuplicatedCostItems, excludedDuplicateCostIds, costBlockers, and proposalStatus; increment state.revision once. Preserve every prior instruction authority finding, drawing scope, field event, schedule basis, and cost attribution. Recompute attributedCostIds as the union of edition nonDuplicatedCostItems. Recompute unresolvedCostIds from costs.unresolvedIds plus prior unresolved IDs not resolved by this edition. Set currentSourceKey to sourceKey and return { ...packet, state }.
